    {
      "id": "eco-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "One economy for everything",
      "number": "01",
      "eyebrow": "Gameplay systems"
    },
    {
      "id": "eco-intro",
      "type": "text",
      "html": "<p>I owned the foundational system loops, using analog paper testing to refine pacing. The pivotal call was eliminating split movement currencies: movement, utility and offensive actions all draw on a single resource pool, so every turn is an economic trade-off and inefficient play is punished on its own terms.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "eco-flow",
      "type": "flow",
      "caption": "One mana pool funds every action. Surplus terrain converts back to mana, so the economy keeps flowing without dead draws.",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "n1",
          "label": "Draw cards"
        },
        {
          "id": "n2",
          "label": "Single mana pool",
          "accent": true
        },
        {
          "id": "n3",
          "label": "Move, attack or defend"
        },
        {
          "id": "n4",
          "label": "Board fills up"
        },
        {
          "id": "n5",
          "label": "Surplus terrain to mana"
        }
